.TH EXTENTS 1
.SH NAME
extents \- the two kinds of sprite extent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/extents
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Extents
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/Extents.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
A sprite is drawn with a three-pixel pen and the box the device context
recorded as actually painted is drawn round it in red.  A key then
replaces the picture with the sprite's own extents, which are measured
from the sprite rather than from anything drawn, and so differ: by the
draw position, and by the pen, which fattens the marks beyond what the
sprite says.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Show the printed extents, then exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/extents.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR spriteedit (1),
.IR wm (1)
